  "notes": "すっぴん is a casual word primarily used in conversation about cosmetics and appearance. It may come from {素|す} (bare/plain) + ぴん (from ピンク or other cosmetic terminology).\n\nREGISTER:\nThis is casual/colloquial language. In more formal contexts, use {素顔|すがお} (natural face) or ノーメイク.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- すっぴんで: without makeup\n- すっぴん{美人|びじん}: a natural beauty\n- すっぴんを{見|み}せる: to show one's bare face",
